{
 "_what": "FROZEN ORACLE — `index.html` as `origin/main` carried it at 407afad, the commit before the eight-signals panel (2026-09-17).",
 "_why": [
  "🔴 THIS FILE IS AN ORACLE, NOT DATA THE PAGE READS. Nothing fetches it. `test_mlb_untouched.py` recomputes these digests from the live `index.html` and fails on any that MOVED.",
  "⛔ `index.html` IS SHARED WITH MLB and MLB IS FROZEN. Sam, 2026-09-12: \"we have mlb perfected we dont need to touch it.\" \"I did not change the MLB call site\" is not proof of that; this is — the same licence `research/bandrow_pre_saidas.js` provides for one shared component, applied to the whole page.",
  "⚠️ IT COVERS EVERY TOP-LEVEL FUNCTION WHOSE NAME DOES NOT START `fb`, WHICH IS MORE THAN THE MLB TABS. `sgn`, `bandRow`, `betLink`, `boardFor`, `freshness` and `priceCell` are SHARED, and teaching one of them about football would be editing MLB through the back door — which the freeze forbids as surely as editing the card.",
  "⚠️ AND EVERY CSS RULE, because a render is the functions AND the rules they draw into. An added selector is allowed; a CHANGED or REMOVED one is not, and neither is a new selector that collides with a frozen one.",
  "⛔ DO NOT REGENERATE IT TO MAKE A RUN GREEN. The moment it tracks the live page it proves nothing. If an MLB-side render must change, that is a decision for Sam and for the freeze, not a fixture edit.",
  "2026-09-22: renderParlays RE-BASELINED, and ONLY it, on Sam's instruction the same day: MLB is unfrozen and the parlay bands lost their ceilings ('1.8- unlimited'; 3x+ above two legs), so the section titles now read 'pays 1.8x or more' / 'pays 3x or more'. Digest a4eab2a6870f4a4dee46d140 -> 3192ca78fc37b7737b736271. Every other frozen digest is unchanged and still pinned at the source commit.",
  "2026-09-23: renderRecord RE-BASELINED, and labN + refitPanel ADDED, on Sam's instruction: MLB was unfrozen 2026-09-22, and the MLB learning task (Sam, 2026-09-23, item 6: 'Every number on the page is labelled MODEL, MARKET or DESCRIPTIVE') puts the champion-vs-challenger panel on the Track Record tab. renderRecord's only change: it fetches data/latest/mlb-refit.json and appends refitPanel(REFIT) after the calibration panel. Digest 20cb8492840fbdc4f7bd1061 -> 0975b831faa24360f95c5ed9. labN and refitPanel are PINNED from birth so a later edit to them is caught too. Every other frozen digest is unchanged and still pinned at the source commit.",
  "2026-09-25: boardFor, gameCard and renderStaleBanner RE-BASELINED, and ONLY they, on Sam's instruction the same day (\"Fix the MATCH, not the test: each game of a doubleheader must get its own odds\"). MLB was unfrozen 2026-09-22. Measured on the 12:08Z board: MLB lists BAL @ NYY game 2 at a 20:10Z placeholder (startTimeTBD) and nearest-first-pitch gave that card GAME 1's odds; the 4h window was also wider than the pair's 3.0h gap. boardFor now matches MLB's gameNumber against the board's first-pitch order first, and falls back to a 90-minute window that refuses a tie and never matches a placeholder time; gameCard's only change passes the game object (`boardFor(away, home, g.gameDate, g)`). Digests boardFor fe1c8d846a5fd62c1bb64096 -> 1992b489b31487aa4e2cef8a, gameCard cd90e58540229fa73446bd5d -> 448c573aec84f22a20240c53. renderStaleBanner's only change: it skips a freshness row marked `page: false` (the new run-status file, data/latest/runs.json, which no tab reads and which reaches Sam through the watchdog instead) — same task, item 3. Digest renderStaleBanner d66926e760beb9a9d51b2c5a -> 9561dbb07cc64ba470cffa24. Every other frozen digest is unchanged and still pinned at the source commit."
 ],
